<important if="you are opening or describing a pull request">
{%- if forge == 'onedev' %}
- The forge is OneDev through `odev`, never `gh`.
- Run `odev pr template` first. `odev pr create` refuses a description that is
  missing a required section.
{%- else %}
- The forge is GitHub through `gh`.
- Fill in every section of `.github/pull_request_template.md` that applies;
  Why, Test plan and Verification are required.
- The weekly refresh (`.github/workflows/update-deps.yml`) opens its PR with the job
  token. Turn on the repo setting "Allow GitHub Actions to create and approve pull
  requests", or it fails. Its PR does not start the gate: close and reopen it.
{%- endif %}
</important>
